+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and the usage it receives covers every provider call the turn made, summed across the rounds that reported: a turn driven through two tool rounds reports both calls' token counts, not the final call alone ([validated by: reports usage summed across every provider call of a two-round turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L55)).
+- A provider that reports no usage on some rounds does not void the rounds that reported: the total still counts them rather than arriving `undefined` or `NaN` ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported when a middle round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- A turn where no provider call reported usage still reports no usage to the hook ([validated by: reports nothing when no round reported usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L90)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what its single provider call reported, the same value the hook has always carried on the common path ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
